From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 23:12:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: qcom: scm: Allow QSEECOM where the device tree has
 qcom,uefisecapp

Allow QSEECOM on a machine whose SCM node has qcom,uefisecapp, as on
the machines in the allowlist. A new laptop then gets its UEFI
variables, and the RTC offset kept among them, through its device tree
alone.

Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
---
 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
index 3eaa4c9cc..677767875 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -2369,7 +2369,8 @@ static int qcom_scm_qseecom_init(struct qcom_scm *scm)
 
 	dev_info(scm->dev, "qseecom: found qseecom with version 0x%x\n", version);
 
-	if (!of_machine_device_match(qcom_scm_qseecom_allowlist)) {
+	if (!of_machine_device_match(qcom_scm_qseecom_allowlist) &&
+	    !of_property_read_bool(scm->dev->of_node, "qcom,uefisecapp")) {
 		dev_info(scm->dev, "qseecom: untested machine, skipping\n");
 		return 0;
 	}
-- 
